# No unsolicited legacy / compatibility layers

Do **not** add backwards-compatible shims unless the user **explicitly** asks to keep old callers working.

## NEVER (unless the user asked for compatibility)

* ❌ Dual names for the same thing (e.g. sort/`CASE` branches for both `student` and `student_name`, `lesson` and `dayAndTime`)
* ❌ “Also accept the old name / old shape” fallbacks, deprecated aliases, or soft-migration wrappers in new or edited code
* ❌ Keeping a removed API surface alive “just in case” while introducing the current one

## ALWAYS

* ✅ One current contract: rename or replace, then update **all** callers to that single surface
* ✅ When editing original migrations (user will `db:reset`): make the schema/RPC match **today’s** callers only — no parallel old keys

Comments must not narrate the removal either — see `comments.mdc`.
